{"ts": "2026-11-19T14:08:42.639290Z", "run_id": "r-20261119T1403Z-ccf1", "unit": "openspec:add-app-shell", "seq": 17, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-009", "id": "Q-009", "status": "answered", "reason": "Read the spec scenario, the Node test and the implementation: the inputs include NaN, Infinity, -1 and 1023.9, which cannot be viewport sizes, and the function has no runtime caller per design.md. I could not read the generated test, so I rely only on the criterion being a pure-function check that the Node test traces, and on the browser threshold being covered by criterion C-425a9f46's scenario with its own test.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "H-91c87ac7", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-006+5", "batch_size": 5, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.569197, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "01a05900c32a6521deca476c2bf5c0db2608382db4f923e1f4520289751f68c3", "checked": [{"ref": "spec:specs/web-shell/spec.md#scenario-the-width-decides-the-layout", "quote": "`shellLayout` gets 0, 1023, 1023.9, 1024, 1280, 1366, `NaN`, `Infinity` and -1", "claim": "The criterion's inputs include values no browser viewport can take."}, {"ref": "web/src/app/shell-layout.test.ts:9", "quote": "const widths = [0, 1023, 1023.9, 1024, 1280, 1366, Number.NaN, Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY, -1];", "claim": "The Node test feeds exactly the nine specified inputs and asserts the nine answers."}, {"ref": "web/src/app/nav-groups.ts:50", "quote": "return widthPx >= 1024 ? \"sidebar\" : \"collapsed\";", "claim": "The implementation answers collapsed for NaN and negatives and sidebar from 1024."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "`shellLayout` has no runtime caller; it states the threshold that the `lg` variant implements", "claim": "The design says the function is not wired to the page, so a browser cannot observe it directly."}, {"ref": "web/src/app/Shell.tsx:108", "quote": "className=\"shrink-0 lg:hidden\"", "claim": "The browser-visible 1024 px threshold is the Tailwind lg variant on the Menu button and nav."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m6b_shell.py:233", "quote": "violations = _open_as(page, base_url, 1023, 800)", "claim": "The browser switch at 1023 and 1024 is checked by the separate menu scenario's test."}]}
